  ('306', '8', '3 Method', 'Inference Pipeline', '31', '학습된 ViT를 이용한 이미지 분류.

---

In model design we follow the original Transformer (Vaswani et al. 2017) as closely as possible.
An advantage of this intentionally simple setup is that scalable NLP Transformer architectures – and their efficient implementations – can be used almost out of the box.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:19.700599+00'),
  ('307', '8', '전체 ViT 구현 Pipeline 정리', '전체 ViT 구현 Pipeline 정리', '32', '전체 ViT 구현 Pipeline 정리', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:19.700599+00'),
  ('308', '9', 'Abstract', '객체 검출을 하나의 회귀 문제로 구성', '0', '“Instead, we frame object detection as a regression problem to spatially separated bounding boxes and associated class probabilities.”

“A single neural network predicts bounding boxes and class probabilities directly from full images in one evaluation.”

We present YOLO, a new approach to object detection. Prior work on object detection repurposes classifiers to perform detection. Instead, we frame object detection as a regression problem to spatially separated bounding boxes and associated class probabilities. A single neural network predicts bounding boxes and class probabilities directly from full images in one evaluation. Since the whole detection pipeline is a single network, it can be optimized end-to-end directly on detection performance.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('309', '9', 'Abstract', '전체 파이프라인의 end-to-end 최적화', '1', '“Since the whole detection pipeline is a single network, it can be optimized end-to-end directly on detection performance.”

We present YOLO, a new approach to object detection. Prior work on object detection repurposes classifiers to perform detection. Instead, we frame object detection as a regression problem to spatially separated bounding boxes and associated class probabilities. A single neural network predicts bounding boxes and class probabilities directly from full images in one evaluation. Since the whole detection pipeline is a single network, it can be optimized end-to-end directly on detection performance.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('310', '9', 'Figure 1 — 448×448 resize', 'Figure 1 — 448×448 resize', '2', '“Our system (1) resizes the input image to 448 × 448…”

Current detection systems repurpose classiﬁers to perform detection. To detect an object, these systems take a classiﬁer for that object and evaluate it at various locations and scales in a test image. Systems like deformable parts models (DPM) use a sliding window approach where the classiﬁer is run at evenly spaced locations over the entire image [10]. More recent approaches like R-CNN use region proposal 1. Resize image. 2. Run convolutional network. 3. Non-max suppression. Dog: 0.30 Person: 0.64 Horse: 0.28 Figure 1: The YOLO Detection System. Processing images with YOLO is simple and straightforward. Our system (1) resizes the input image to 448 × 448, (2) runs a single convolutional network on the image, and (3) thresholds the resulting detections by the model’s conﬁdence.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('311', '9', 'Figure 1 — 한 번의 convolutional network 실행', 'Figure 1 — 한 번의 convolutional network 실행', '3', '“(2) runs a single convolutional network on the image…”

Current detection systems repurpose classiﬁers to perform detection. To detect an object, these systems take a classiﬁer for that object and evaluate it at various locations and scales in a test image. Systems like deformable parts models (DPM) use a sliding window approach where the classiﬁer is run at evenly spaced locations over the entire image [10]. More recent approaches like R-CNN use region proposal 1. Resize image. 2. Run convolutional network. 3. Non-max suppression. Dog: 0.30 Person: 0.64 Horse: 0.28 Figure 1: The YOLO Detection System. Processing images with YOLO is simple and straightforward. Our system (1) resizes the input image to 448 × 448, (2) runs a single convolutional network on the image, and (3) thresholds the resulting detections by the model’s conﬁdence.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('312', '9', 'Figure 1 — confidence threshold와 NMS', 'Figure 1 — confidence threshold와 NMS', '4', '“(3) thresholds the resulting detections by the model’s confidence.”

“Non-max suppression.”

Current detection systems repurpose classiﬁers to perform detection. To detect an object, these systems take a classiﬁer for that object and evaluate it at various locations and scales in a test image. Systems like deformable parts models (DPM) use a sliding window approach where the classiﬁer is run at evenly spaced locations over the entire image [10]. More recent approaches like R-CNN use region proposal 1. Resize image. 2. Run convolutional network. 3. Non-max suppression. Dog: 0.30 Person: 0.64 Horse: 0.28 Figure 1: The YOLO Detection System. Processing images with YOLO is simple and straightforward. Our system (1) resizes the input image to 448 × 448, (2) runs a single convolutional network on the image, and (3) thresholds the resulting detections by the model’s conﬁdence.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('313', '9', 'Abstract', '실시간 속도 45 FPS', '5', '“Our base YOLO model processes images in real-time at 45 frames per second.”

Our unified architecture is extremely fast. Our base YOLO model processes images in real-time at 45 frames per second. A smaller version of the network, Fast YOLO, processes an astounding 155 frames per second while still achieving double the mAP of other real-time detectors. Compared to state-of-the-art detection systems, YOLO makes more localization errors but is less likely to predict false positives on background. Finally, YOLO learns very general representations of objects. It outperforms other detection methods, including DPM and R-CNN, when generalizing from natural images to other domains like artwork.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('314', '9', 'Abstract', 'Fast YOLO 155 FPS', '6', '“Fast YOLO processes an astounding 155 frames per second…”

Our unified architecture is extremely fast. Our base YOLO model processes images in real-time at 45 frames per second. A smaller version of the network, Fast YOLO, processes an astounding 155 frames per second while still achieving double the mAP of other real-time detectors. Compared to state-of-the-art detection systems, YOLO makes more localization errors but is less likely to predict false positives on background. Finally, YOLO learns very general representations of objects. It outperforms other detection methods, including DPM and R-CNN, when generalizing from natural images to other domains like artwork.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('315', '9', '1 Introduction', '전체 이미지의 global context 사용', '7', '“YOLO sees the entire image during training and test time so it implicitly encodes contextual information about classes as well as their appearance.”

Second, YOLO reasons globally about the image when making predictions. Unlike sliding window and region proposal-based techniques, YOLO sees the entire image during training and test time so it implicitly encodes contextual information about classes as well as their appearance. Fast R-CNN, a top detection method DBLP:journals/corr/Girshick15, mistakes background patches in an image for objects because it can’t see the larger context. YOLO makes less than half the number of background errors compared to Fast R-CNN.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('316', '9', '1 Introduction', 'Sliding-window와 R-CNN 설명', '8', '“DPM use a sliding window approach…”

“R-CNN use region proposal methods…”

Current detection systems repurpose classifiers to perform detection. To detect an object, these systems take a classifier for that object and evaluate it at various locations and scales in a test image. Systems like deformable parts models (DPM) use a sliding window approach where the classifier is run at evenly spaced locations over the entire image lsvm-pami.', '1', '1', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('317', '9', '2 Unified Detection', '하나의 network로 detection 요소 통합', '9', '“We unify the separate components of object detection into a single neural network.”

“It also predicts all bounding boxes across all classes for an image simultaneously.”

We unify the separate components of object detection into a single neural network. Our network uses features from the entire image to predict each bounding box. It also predicts all bounding boxes across all classes for an image simultaneously. This means our network reasons globally about the full image and all the objects in the image. The YOLO design enables end-to-end training and real-time speeds while maintaining high average precision.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('318', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'S×S grid', '10', E'“Our system divides the input image into an S × S grid.”

Our system divides the input image into an S\\times S grid. If the center of an object falls into a grid cell, that grid cell is responsible for detecting that object.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('319', '9', '2 Unified Detection', '객체 중심이 위치한 cell이 검출 책임', '11', E'“If the center of an object falls into a grid cell, that grid cell is responsible for detecting that object.”

Our system divides the input image into an S\\times S grid. If the center of an object falls into a grid cell, that grid cell is responsible for detecting that object.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('320', '9', '2 Unified Detection', '각 cell이 B개 bounding box와 confidence 예측', '12', E'“Each grid cell predicts B bounding boxes and confidence scores for those boxes.”

Each grid cell predicts B bounding boxes and confidence scores for those boxes. These confidence scores reflect how confident the model is that the box contains an object and also how accurate it thinks the box is that it predicts. Formally we define confidence as \\Pr(\\textrm{Object})*\\textrm{IOU}_{\\textrm{pred}}^{\\textrm{truth}} . If no object exists in that cell, the confidence scores should be zero. Otherwise we want the confidence score to equal the intersection over union (IOU) between the predicted box and the ground truth.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('321', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'Confidence = Pr(Object) × IoU', '13', E'“Formally we define confidence as Pr(Object) ∗ IOU…”

“If no object exists in that cell, the confidence scores should be zero.”

Each grid cell predicts B bounding boxes and confidence scores for those boxes. These confidence scores reflect how confident the model is that the box contains an object and also how accurate it thinks the box is that it predicts. Formally we define confidence as \\Pr(\\textrm{Object})*\\textrm{IOU}_{\\textrm{pred}}^{\\textrm{truth}} . If no object exists in that cell, the confidence scores should be zero. Otherwise we want the confidence score to equal the intersection over union (IOU) between the predicted box and the ground truth.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('322', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'x, y, w, h, confidence 다섯 예측값', '14', '“Each bounding box consists of 5 predictions: x, y, w, h, and confidence.”

Each bounding box consists of 5 predictions: x , y , w , h , and confidence. The (x,y) coordinates represent the center of the box relative to the bounds of the grid cell. The width and height are predicted relative to the whole image. Finally the confidence prediction represents the IOU between the predicted box and any ground truth box.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('323', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'x, y는 cell-relative offset', '15', '“The (x, y) coordinates represent the center of the box relative to the bounds of the grid cell.”

Each bounding box consists of 5 predictions: x , y , w , h , and confidence. The (x,y) coordinates represent the center of the box relative to the bounds of the grid cell. The width and height are predicted relative to the whole image. Finally the confidence prediction represents the IOU between the predicted box and any ground truth box.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('324', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'w, h는 전체 이미지 기준', '16', '“The width and height are predicted relative to the whole image.”

Each bounding box consists of 5 predictions: x , y , w , h , and confidence. The (x,y) coordinates represent the center of the box relative to the bounds of the grid cell. The width and height are predicted relative to the whole image. Finally the confidence prediction represents the IOU between the predicted box and any ground truth box.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('325', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'Conditional class probability', '17', E'“Each grid cell also predicts C conditional class probabilities, Pr(Class_i|Object).”

Each grid cell also predicts C conditional class probabilities, \\Pr(\\textrm{Class}_{i}|\\textrm{Object}) . These probabilities are conditioned on the grid cell containing an object. We only predict one set of class probabilities per grid cell, regardless of the number of boxes B .', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('326', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'Box별 class probability가 아니라 cell당 한 세트', '18', E'“We only predict one set of class probabilities per grid cell, regardless of the number of boxes B.”

Each grid cell also predicts C conditional class probabilities, \\Pr(\\textrm{Class}_{i}|\\textrm{Object}) . These probabilities are conditioned on the grid cell containing an object. We only predict one set of class probabilities per grid cell, regardless of the number of boxes B .', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('327', '9', 'Equation (1) — class-specific confidence', 'Equation (1) — class-specific confidence', '19', 'Equation (1) — class-specific confidence

Finally the conﬁdence prediction represents the IOU between the predicted box and any ground truth box. Each grid cell also predicts C conditional class probabilities, Pr(Classi|Object). These probabilities are conditioned on the grid cell containing an object. We only predict one set of class probabilities per grid cell, regardless of the number of boxesB. At test time we multiply the conditional class probabilities and the individual box conﬁdence predictions, Pr(Classi|Object)∗ Pr(Object)∗ IOUtruth pred = Pr( Classi)∗ IOUtruth pred (1) which gives us class-speciﬁc conﬁdence scores for each box. These scores encode both the probability of that class appearing in the box and how well the predicted box ﬁts the object.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('328', '9', '2 Unified Detection', 'Figure 2 — `S×S×(B×5+C)` tensor', '20', E'“These predictions are encoded as an S × S × (B ∗ 5 + C) tensor.”

“For PASCAL VOC, S=7, B=2, C=20. Our final prediction is a 7×7×30 tensor.”

For evaluating YOLO on Pascal VOC, we use S=7 , B=2 . Pascal VOC has 20 labelled classes so C=20 . Our final prediction is a 7\\times 7\\times 30 tensor.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('329', '9', '2.1 Network Design', '24 convolution + 2 fully connected layers', '21', E'“Our network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers.”

Our network architecture is inspired by the GoogLeNet model for image classification DBLP:journals/corr/SzegedyLJSRAEVR14. Our network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers. Instead of the inception modules used by GoogLeNet, we simply use 1\\times 1 reduction layers followed by 3\\times 3 convolutional layers, similar to Lin et al DBLP:journals/corr/LinCY13. The full network is shown in Figure 3.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('330', '9', '2.1 Network Design', '1×1 reduction 뒤 3×3 convolution', '22', E'“We simply use 1 × 1 reduction layers followed by 3 × 3 convolutional layers.”

Our network architecture is inspired by the GoogLeNet model for image classification DBLP:journals/corr/SzegedyLJSRAEVR14. Our network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers. Instead of the inception modules used by GoogLeNet, we simply use 1\\times 1 reduction layers followed by 3\\times 3 convolutional layers, similar to Lin et al DBLP:journals/corr/LinCY13. The full network is shown in Figure 3.', '2', '2', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('331', '9', 'Figure 3 — 입력 448×448', 'Figure 3 — 입력 448×448', '23', '“448 × 448 × 3”

448 448 3 7 7 Conv. Layer 7x7x64-s-2 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 112 112 192 3 3 56 56 256 Conn. Layer 4096 Conn. LayerConv. Layer 3x3x192 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 Conv. Layers 1x1x128 3x3x256 1x1x256 3x3x512 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 28 28 512 Conv. Layers 1x1x256 3x3x512 1x1x512 3x3x1024 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 14 14 1024 Conv. Layers 1x1x512 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 3x3x1024-s-2 3 3 7 7 1024 7 7 1024 7 7 30 } ×4 } ×2 Conv. Layers 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 Figure 3: The Architecture. Our detection network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers. Alternating 1 × 1 convolutional layers reduce the features space from preceding layers. We pretrain the convolutional layers on the ImageNet classiﬁcation task at half the resolution (224 × 224 input image) and then double the resolution for detection.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('332', '9', '첫 번째 7×7 convolution, 64 filters, stride 2', '첫 번째 7×7 convolution, 64 filters, stride 2', '24', '“Conv. Layer 7x7x64-s-2”

448 448 3 7 7 Conv. Layer 7x7x64-s-2 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 112 112 192 3 3 56 56 256 Conn. Layer 4096 Conn. LayerConv. Layer 3x3x192 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 Conv. Layers 1x1x128 3x3x256 1x1x256 3x3x512 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 28 28 512 Conv. Layers 1x1x256 3x3x512 1x1x512 3x3x1024 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 14 14 1024 Conv. Layers 1x1x512 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 3x3x1024-s-2 3 3 7 7 1024 7 7 1024 7 7 30 } ×4 } ×2 Conv. Layers 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 Figure 3: The Architecture. Our detection network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers. Alternating 1 × 1 convolutional layers reduce the features space from preceding layers. We pretrain the convolutional layers on the ImageNet classiﬁcation task at half the resolution (224 × 224 input image) and then double the resolution for detection.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('333', '9', '2×2 max pooling stride 2', '2×2 max pooling stride 2', '25', '“Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2”

448 448 3 7 7 Conv. Layer 7x7x64-s-2 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 112 112 192 3 3 56 56 256 Conn. Layer 4096 Conn. LayerConv. Layer 3x3x192 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 Conv. Layers 1x1x128 3x3x256 1x1x256 3x3x512 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 28 28 512 Conv. Layers 1x1x256 3x3x512 1x1x512 3x3x1024 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 14 14 1024 Conv. Layers 1x1x512 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 3x3x1024-s-2 3 3 7 7 1024 7 7 1024 7 7 30 } ×4 } ×2 Conv. Layers 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 Figure 3: The Architecture. Our detection network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers. Alternating 1 × 1 convolutional layers reduce the features space from preceding layers. We pretrain the convolutional layers on the ImageNet classiﬁcation task at half the resolution (224 × 224 input image) and then double the resolution for detection.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('334', '9', '3×3×192 convolution', '3×3×192 convolution', '26', '“Conv. Layer 3x3x192”

448 448 3 7 7 Conv. Layer 7x7x64-s-2 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 112 112 192 3 3 56 56 256 Conn. Layer 4096 Conn. LayerConv. Layer 3x3x192 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 Conv. Layers 1x1x128 3x3x256 1x1x256 3x3x512 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 28 28 512 Conv. Layers 1x1x256 3x3x512 1x1x512 3x3x1024 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 14 14 1024 Conv. Layers 1x1x512 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 3x3x1024-s-2 3 3 7 7 1024 7 7 1024 7 7 30 } ×4 } ×2 Conv. Layers 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 Figure 3: The Architecture. Our detection network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers. Alternating 1 × 1 convolutional layers reduce the features space from preceding layers. We pretrain the convolutional layers on the ImageNet classiﬁcation task at half the resolution (224 × 224 input image) and then double the resolution for detection.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('335', '9', 'Figure 3 반복 블록', 'Figure 3 반복 블록', '27', '“1x1x256 → 3x3x512” ×4

“1x1x512 → 3x3x1024” ×2

448 448 3 7 7 Conv. Layer 7x7x64-s-2 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 112 112 192 3 3 56 56 256 Conn. Layer 4096 Conn. LayerConv. Layer 3x3x192 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 Conv. Layers 1x1x128 3x3x256 1x1x256 3x3x512 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 28 28 512 Conv. Layers 1x1x256 3x3x512 1x1x512 3x3x1024 Maxpool Layer 2x2-s-2 3 3 14 14 1024 Conv. Layers 1x1x512 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 3x3x1024-s-2 3 3 7 7 1024 7 7 1024 7 7 30 } ×4 } ×2 Conv. Layers 3x3x1024 3x3x1024 Figure 3: The Architecture. Our detection network has 24 convolutional layers followed by 2 fully connected layers. Alternating 1 × 1 convolutional layers reduce the features space from preceding layers. We pretrain the convolutional layers on the ImageNet classiﬁcation task at half the resolution (224 × 224 input image) and then double the resolution for detection.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('336', '9', '2.2 Training', 'ImageNet에서 224×224로 pretraining', '28', '“We pretrain the convolutional layers on the ImageNet classification task at half the resolution (224 × 224 input image).”

We pretrain our convolutional layers on the ImageNet 1000-class competition dataset ILSVRC15. For pretraining we use the first 20 convolutional layers from Figure 3 followed by a average-pooling layer and a fully connected layer. We train this network for approximately a week and achieve a single crop top-5 accuracy of 88% on the ImageNet 2012 validation set, comparable to the GoogLeNet models in Caffe’s Model Zoo zoo. We use the Darknet framework for all training and inference darknet13.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('337', '9', '2.2 Training', 'ImageNet 1000-class pretraining', '29', '“For pretraining we use the first 20 convolutional layers … followed by an average-pooling layer and a fully connected layer.”

We pretrain our convolutional layers on the ImageNet 1000-class competition dataset ILSVRC15. For pretraining we use the first 20 convolutional layers from Figure 3 followed by a average-pooling layer and a fully connected layer. We train this network for approximately a week and achieve a single crop top-5 accuracy of 88% on the ImageNet 2012 validation set, comparable to the GoogLeNet models in Caffe’s Model Zoo zoo. We use the Darknet framework for all training and inference darknet13.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('338', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Detection용으로 네 convolution과 두 connected layer 추가', '30', E'“We add four convolutional layers and two fully connected layers with randomly initialized weights.”

We then convert the model to perform detection. Ren et al. show that adding both convolutional and connected layers to pretrained networks can improve performance DBLP:journals/corr/RenHGZ015. Following their example, we add four convolutional layers and two fully connected layers with randomly initialized weights. Detection often requires fine-grained visual information so we increase the input resolution of the network from 224\\times 224 to 448\\times 448 .', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('339', '9', '2.2 Training', '224에서 448로 해상도 증가', '31', E'“We increase the input resolution of the network from 224 × 224 to 448 × 448.”

We then convert the model to perform detection. Ren et al. show that adding both convolutional and connected layers to pretrained networks can improve performance DBLP:journals/corr/RenHGZ015. Following their example, we add four convolutional layers and two fully connected layers with randomly initialized weights. Detection often requires fine-grained visual information so we increase the input resolution of the network from 224\\times 224 to 448\\times 448 .', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('340', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Width와 height를 0~1로 정규화', '32', '“We normalize the bounding box width and height by the image width and height so that they fall between 0 and 1.”

Our final layer predicts both class probabilities and bounding box coordinates. We normalize the bounding box width and height by the image width and height so that they fall between 0 and 1. We parametrize the bounding box x and y coordinates to be offsets of a particular grid cell location so they are also bounded between 0 and 1.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('341', '9', '2.2 Training', '최종 layer는 linear activation', '33', '“We use a linear activation function for the final layer.”

We use a linear activation function for the final layer and all other layers use the following leaky rectified linear activation:', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('342', '9', '나머지 layer는 Leaky ReLU 0.1', '나머지 layer는 Leaky ReLU 0.1', '34', 'Darknet의 Leaky ReLU 예상 구현:

Following their example, we add four convolutional layers and two fully connected layers with randomly initialized weights. Detection often requires ﬁne-grained visual information so we increase the input resolution of the network from 224× 224 to 448× 448. Our ﬁnal layer predicts both class probabilities and bounding box coordinates. We normalize the bounding box width and height by the image width and height so that they fall between 0 and 1. We parametrize the bounding box x andy coordinates to be offsets of a particular grid cell location so they are also bounded between 0 and 1. We use a linear activation function for the ﬁnal layer and all other layers use the following leaky rectiﬁed linear activation: φ(x) = { x, ifx> 0 0.1x, otherwise (2) We optimize for sum-squared error in the output of our model.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('343', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Sum-squared error 사용', '35', '“We optimize for sum-squared error in the output of our model.”

We optimize for sum-squared error in the output of our model. We use sum-squared error because it is easy to optimize, however it does not perfectly align with our goal of maximizing average precision. It weights localization error equally with classification error which may not be ideal. Also, in every image many grid cells do not contain any object. This pushes the “confidence” scores of those cells towards zero, often overpowering the gradient from cells that do contain objects. This can lead to model instability, causing training to diverge early on.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('344', '9', '`λcoord=5`, `λnoobj=0.5`', '`λcoord=5`, `λnoobj=0.5`', '36', '“We set λcoord = 5 and λnoobj = .5.”

It weights localization error equally with classiﬁcation error which may not be ideal. Also, in every image many grid cells do not contain any object. This pushes the “conﬁdence” scores of those cells towards zero, often overpowering the gradient from cells that do contain objects. This can lead to model instability, causing training to diverge early on. To remedy this, we increase the loss from bounding box coordinate predictions and decrease the loss from conﬁdence predictions for boxes that don’t contain objects. We use two parameters,λcoord andλnoobj to accomplish this. We setλcoord = 5 andλnoobj =.5. Sum-squared error also equally weights errors in large boxes and small boxes. Our error metric should reﬂect that small deviations in large boxes matter less than in small boxes.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('345', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Width와 height의 square root 예측', '37', '“We predict the square root of the bounding box width and height instead of the width and height directly.”

Sum-squared error also equally weights errors in large boxes and small boxes. Our error metric should reflect that small deviations in large boxes matter less than in small boxes. To partially address this we predict the square root of the bounding box width and height instead of the width and height directly.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('346', '9', '2.2 Training', '가장 높은 IoU predictor가 책임', '38', '“We assign one predictor to be responsible … based on which prediction has the highest current IOU with the ground truth.”

YOLO predicts multiple bounding boxes per grid cell. At training time we only want one bounding box predictor to be responsible for each object. We assign one predictor to be “responsible” for predicting an object based on which prediction has the highest current IOU with the ground truth. This leads to specialization between the bounding box predictors. Each predictor gets better at predicting certain sizes, aspect ratios, or classes of object, improving overall recall.', '3', '3', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('347', '9', 'Equation (3) — 전체 YOLO loss', 'Equation (3) — 전체 YOLO loss', '39', '공식 cfg의 가중치:

2.4. Limitations of YOLO YOLO imposes strong spatial constraints on bounding box predictions since each grid cell only predicts two boxes and can only have one class. This spatial constraint limits the number of nearby objects that our model can predict. Our model struggles with small objects that appear in groups, such as ﬂocks of birds. Since our model learns to predict bounding boxes from data, it struggles to generalize to objects in new or unusual aspect ratios or conﬁgurations. Our model also uses relatively coarse features for predicting bounding boxes since our architecture has multiple downsampling layers from the input image. Finally, while we train on a loss function that approximates detection performance, our loss function treats errors the same in small bounding boxes versus large bounding boxes.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('348', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Classification loss는 object cell에만 적용', '40', '“The loss function only penalizes classification error if an object is present in that grid cell.”

Note that the loss function only penalizes classification error if an object is present in that grid cell (hence the conditional class probability discussed earlier). It also only penalizes bounding box coordinate error if that predictor is “responsible” for the ground truth box (i.e. has the highest IOU of any predictor in that grid cell).', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('349', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Coordinate loss는 responsible predictor에만 적용', '41', '“It also only penalizes bounding box coordinate error if that predictor is responsible for the ground truth box.”

Note that the loss function only penalizes classification error if an object is present in that grid cell (hence the conditional class probability discussed earlier). It also only penalizes bounding box coordinate error if that predictor is “responsible” for the ground truth box (i.e. has the highest IOU of any predictor in that grid cell).', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('350', '9', '2.2 Training', '135 epochs', '42', '“We train the network for about 135 epochs…”

We train the network for about 135 epochs on the training and validation data sets from Pascal VOC 2007 and 2012. When testing on 2012 we also include the VOC 2007 test data for training. Throughout training we use a batch size of 64, a momentum of 0.9 and a decay of 0.0005 .', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('351', '9', '2.2 Training', 'PASCAL VOC 2007·2012 학습', '43', '“On the training and validation data sets from PASCAL VOC 2007 and 2012.”

We train the network for about 135 epochs on the training and validation data sets from Pascal VOC 2007 and 2012. When testing on 2012 we also include the VOC 2007 test data for training. Throughout training we use a batch size of 64, a momentum of 0.9 and a decay of 0.0005 .', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('352', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Batch size 64', '44', '“Throughout training we use a batch size of 64…”

We train the network for about 135 epochs on the training and validation data sets from Pascal VOC 2007 and 2012. When testing on 2012 we also include the VOC 2007 test data for training. Throughout training we use a batch size of 64, a momentum of 0.9 and a decay of 0.0005 .', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('353', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Momentum 0.9', '45', '“A momentum of 0.9…”

We train the network for about 135 epochs on the training and validation data sets from Pascal VOC 2007 and 2012. When testing on 2012 we also include the VOC 2007 test data for training. Throughout training we use a batch size of 64, a momentum of 0.9 and a decay of 0.0005 .', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('354', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Weight decay 0.0005', '46', '“A decay of 0.0005.”

We train the network for about 135 epochs on the training and validation data sets from Pascal VOC 2007 and 2012. When testing on 2012 we also include the VOC 2007 test data for training. Throughout training we use a batch size of 64, a momentum of 0.9 and a decay of 0.0005 .', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('355', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Learning-rate schedule', '47', '“Slowly raise the learning rate from 10⁻³ to 10⁻².”

“Continue with 10⁻² for 75 epochs, then 10⁻³ for 30 epochs, and finally 10⁻⁴ for 30 epochs.”

Our learning rate schedule is as follows: For the first epochs we slowly raise the learning rate from 10^{-3} to 10^{-2} . If we start at a high learning rate our model often diverges due to unstable gradients. We continue training with 10^{-2} for 75 epochs, then 10^{-3} for 30 epochs, and finally 10^{-4} for 30 epochs.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('356', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Dropout 0.5', '48', '“A dropout layer with rate=.5 after the first connected layer…”

To avoid overfitting we use dropout and extensive data augmentation. A dropout layer with rate = .5 after the first connected layer prevents co-adaptation between layers hinton2012improving. For data augmentation we introduce random scaling and translations of up to 20% of the original image size. We also randomly adjust the exposure and saturation of the image by up to a factor of 1.5 in the HSV color space.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('357', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Random scaling·translation 최대 20%', '49', '“Random scaling and translations of up to 20% of the original image size.”

To avoid overfitting we use dropout and extensive data augmentation. A dropout layer with rate = .5 after the first connected layer prevents co-adaptation between layers hinton2012improving. For data augmentation we introduce random scaling and translations of up to 20% of the original image size. We also randomly adjust the exposure and saturation of the image by up to a factor of 1.5 in the HSV color space.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('358', '9', '2.2 Training', 'Exposure와 saturation factor 1.5', '50', '“Randomly adjust the exposure and saturation … by up to a factor of 1.5 in HSV color space.”

To avoid overfitting we use dropout and extensive data augmentation. A dropout layer with rate = .5 after the first connected layer prevents co-adaptation between layers hinton2012improving. For data augmentation we introduce random scaling and translations of up to 20% of the original image size. We also randomly adjust the exposure and saturation of the image by up to a factor of 1.5 in the HSV color space.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('359', '9', '2.3 Inference', '한 번의 network evaluation', '51', '“Predicting detections for a test image only requires one network evaluation.”

Just like in training, predicting detections for a test image only requires one network evaluation. On Pascal VOC the network predicts 98 bounding boxes per image and class probabilities for each box. YOLO is extremely fast at test time since it only requires a single network evaluation, unlike classifier-based methods.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('360', '9', '2.3 Inference', '이미지당 98개 bounding box', '52', '“The network predicts 98 bounding boxes per image…”

Just like in training, predicting detections for a test image only requires one network evaluation. On Pascal VOC the network predicts 98 bounding boxes per image and class probabilities for each box. YOLO is extremely fast at test time since it only requires a single network evaluation, unlike classifier-based methods.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('361', '9', '2.3 Inference', 'Non-maximal suppression', '53', '“Non-maximal suppression can be used to fix these multiple detections.”

The grid design enforces spatial diversity in the bounding box predictions. Often it is clear which grid cell an object falls in to and the network only predicts one box for each object. However, some large objects or objects near the border of multiple cells can be well localized by multiple cells. Non-maximal suppression can be used to fix these multiple detections. While not critical to performance as it is for R-CNN or DPM, non-maximal suppression adds 2-3% in mAP.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('362', '9', '2.3 Inference', 'NMS로 2~3% mAP 개선', '54', '“Non-maximal suppression adds 2–3% in mAP.”

The grid design enforces spatial diversity in the bounding box predictions. Often it is clear which grid cell an object falls in to and the network only predicts one box for each object. However, some large objects or objects near the border of multiple cells can be well localized by multiple cells. Non-maximal suppression can be used to fix these multiple detections. While not critical to performance as it is for R-CNN or DPM, non-maximal suppression adds 2-3% in mAP.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('363', '9', '2.4 Limitations of YOLO', 'YOLO의 small-object 한계', '55', '“Our model struggles with small objects that appear in groups…”

YOLO imposes strong spatial constraints on bounding box predictions since each grid cell only predicts two boxes and can only have one class. This spatial constraint limits the number of nearby objects that our model can predict. Our model struggles with small objects that appear in groups, such as flocks of birds.', '4', '4', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('364', '9', '3 Comparison to Other Detection Systems', 'DPM과 비교', '56', '“DPM uses a disjoint pipeline…”

“Our system replaces all of these disparate parts with a single convolutional neural network.”

Deformable parts models. Deformable parts models (DPM) use a sliding window approach to object detection lsvm-pami. DPM uses a disjoint pipeline to extract static features, classify regions, predict bounding boxes for high scoring regions, etc. Our system replaces all of these disparate parts with a single convolutional neural network. The network performs feature extraction, bounding box prediction, non-maximal suppression, and contextual reasoning all concurrently. Instead of static features, the network trains the features in-line and optimizes them for the detection task. Our unified architecture leads to a faster, more accurate model than DPM.', '5', '5', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('365', '9', '3 Comparison to Other Detection Systems', 'R-CNN의 약 2000 proposal과 YOLO의 98 box', '57', '“Only 98 per image compared to about 2000 from Selective Search.”

YOLO shares some similarities with R-CNN. Each grid cell proposes potential bounding boxes and scores those boxes using convolutional features. However, our system puts spatial constraints on the grid cell proposals which helps mitigate multiple detections of the same object. Our system also proposes far fewer bounding boxes, only 98 per image compared to about 2000 from Selective Search. Finally, our system combines these individual components into a single, jointly optimized model.', '5', '5', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('366', '9', '3 Comparison to Other Detection Systems', '여러 class를 동시에 검출하는 general-purpose detector', '58', '“YOLO is a general purpose detector that learns to detect a variety of objects simultaneously.”

Detectors for single classes like faces or people can be highly optimized since they have to deal with much less variation viola2004robust. YOLO is a general purpose detector that learns to detect a variety of objects simultaneously.', '5', '5', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('367', '9', 'Table 1 — mAP와 FPS 비교', 'Table 1 — mAP와 FPS 비교', '59', 'Table 1 — mAP와 FPS 비교

Real-Time Detectors Train mAP FPS 100Hz DPM [31] 2007 16.0 100 30Hz DPM [31] 2007 26.1 30 Fast YOLO 2007+2012 52.7 155 YOLO 2007+2012 63.4 45 Less Than Real-Time Fastest DPM [38] 2007 30.4 15 R-CNN Minus R [20] 2007 53.5 6 Fast R-CNN [14] 2007+2012 70.0 0.5 Faster R-CNN VGG-16[28] 2007+2012 73.2 7 Faster R-CNN ZF [28] 2007+2012 62.1 18 YOLO VGG-16 2007+2012 66.4 21 Table 1: Real-Time Systems on PASCAL VOC 2007. Comparing the performance and speed of fast detectors. Fast YOLO is the fastest detector on record for P ASCAL VOC detection and is still twice as accurate as any other real-time detector. YOLO is 10 mAP more accurate than the fast version while still well above real-time in speed. R-CNN, it still falls short of real-time and takes a signiﬁcant accuracy hit from not having good proposals.', '6', '6', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('368', '9', 'Error Analysis 기준', 'Error Analysis 기준', '60', 'Error Analysis 기준

Fast R-CNN speeds up the classiﬁcation stage of R-CNN but it still relies on selective search which can take around 2 seconds per image to generate bounding box proposals. Thus it has high mAP but at 0.5 fps it is still far from realtime. The recent Faster R-CNN replaces selective search with a neural network to propose bounding boxes, similar to Szegedy et al. [8] In our tests, their most accurate model achieves 7 fps while a smaller, less accurate one runs at 18 fps. The VGG-16 version of Faster R-CNN is 10 mAP higher but is also 6 times slower than YOLO. The ZeilerFergus Faster R-CNN is only 2.5 times slower than YOLO but is also less accurate. 4.2. VOC 2007 Error Analysis To further examine the differences between YOLO and state-of-the-art detectors, we look at a detailed breakdown of results on VOC 2007.', '6', '6', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('369', '9', '4.3 Combining Fast R-CNN and YOLO', 'Fast R-CNN 결과를 YOLO로 재점수화', '61', '“For every bounding box that R-CNN predicts we check to see if YOLO predicts a similar box.”

“We give that prediction a boost based on the probability predicted by YOLO and the overlap…”

YOLO makes far fewer background mistakes than Fast R-CNN. By using YOLO to eliminate background detections from Fast R-CNN we get a significant boost in performance. For every bounding box that R-CNN predicts we check to see if YOLO predicts a similar box. If it does, we give that prediction a boost based on the probability predicted by YOLO and the overlap between the two boxes.', '6', '6', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('370', '9', '4.4 VOC 2012 Results', 'VOC 2012 mAP 57.9', '62', '“On the VOC 2012 test set, YOLO scores 57.9% mAP.”

On the VOC 2012 test set, YOLO scores 57.9% mAP. This is lower than the current state of the art, closer to the original R-CNN using VGG-16, see Table 3. Our system struggles with small objects compared to its closest competitors. On categories like bottle, sheep, and tv/monitor YOLO scores 8-10% lower than R-CNN or Feature Edit. However, on other categories like cat and train YOLO achieves higher performance.', '7', '7', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('371', '9', '4.4 VOC 2012 Results', 'Small object class 성능 저하', '63', '“On categories like bottle, sheep, and tv/monitor YOLO scores 8–10% lower…”

On the VOC 2012 test set, YOLO scores 57.9% mAP. This is lower than the current state of the art, closer to the original R-CNN using VGG-16, see Table 3. Our system struggles with small objects compared to its closest competitors. On categories like bottle, sheep, and tv/monitor YOLO scores 8-10% lower than R-CNN or Feature Edit. However, on other categories like cat and train YOLO achieves higher performance.', '7', '7', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('372', '9', '4.5 Generalizability: Person Detection in Artwork', 'Artwork generalization', '64', '“We compare YOLO … on the Picasso Dataset and the People-Art Dataset.”

Academic datasets for object detection draw the training and testing data from the same distribution. In real-world applications it is hard to predict all possible use cases and the test data can diverge from what the system has seen before cai2015cross.
We compare YOLO to other detection systems on the Picasso Dataset ginosar2014detecting and the People-Art Dataset cai2015cross, two datasets for testing person detection on artwork.', '7', '7', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('373', '9', 'Figure 5 — Precision-Recall curve, AP, F1', 'Figure 5 — Precision-Recall curve, AP, F1', '65', 'Figure 5 — Precision-Recall curve, AP, F1

Poselets RCNN D&T Humans DPM YOLO (a) Picasso Dataset precision-recall curves. VOC 2007 Picasso People-Art AP AP Best F1 AP YOLO 59.2 53.3 0.590 45 R-CNN 54.2 10.4 0.226 26 DPM 43.2 37.8 0.458 32 Poselets [2] 36.5 17.8 0.271 D&T [4] - 1.9 0.051 (b) Quantitative results on the VOC 2007, Picasso, and People-Art Datasets. The Picasso Dataset evaluates on both AP and best F1 score. Figure 5: Generalization results on Picasso and People-Art datasets. Figure 6: Qualitative Results. YOLO running on sample artwork and natural images from the internet. It is mostly accurate although it does think one person is an airplane. including the time to fetch images from the camera and display the detections.', '8', '8', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('374', '9', '5 Real-Time Detection In The Wild', 'Webcam 실시간 detection', '66', '“We connect YOLO to a webcam and verify that it maintains real-time performance…”

YOLO is a fast, accurate object detector, making it ideal for computer vision applications. We connect YOLO to a webcam and verify that it maintains real-time performance, including the time to fetch images from the camera and display the detections.', '8', '8', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('375', '9', '5 Real-Time Detection In The Wild', 'Tracking처럼 동작', '67', '“While YOLO processes images individually, when attached to a webcam it functions like a tracking system…”

The resulting system is interactive and engaging. While YOLO processes images individually, when attached to a webcam it functions like a tracking system, detecting objects as they move around and change in appearance. A demo of the system and the source code can be found on our project website: http://pjreddie.com/yolo/.', '8', '8', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00'),
  ('376', '9', '6 Conclusion', 'Conclusion — full-image joint training', '68', '“Our model … can be trained directly on full images.”

“The entire model is trained jointly.”

We introduce YOLO, a unified model for object detection. Our model is simple to construct and can be trained directly on full images. Unlike classifier-based approaches, YOLO is trained on a loss function that directly corresponds to detection performance and the entire model is trained jointly.', '8', '8', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:04:20.096398+00');

